  "body": "https://html.spec.whatwg.org/#flow-content-3 has:\r\n\r\n```css\r\ndialog {\r\n  background: white;\r\n  color: black;\r\n}\r\n```\r\n\r\nThat's what Firefox implements to the letter, but:\r\n\r\n * That doesn't account for dark mode (Chromium uses `-internal-light-dark(..)` instead).\r\n * That doesn't account for high contrast use cases (https://bugzilla.mozilla.org/show_bug.cgi?id=1761611).\r\n\r\nTo fix the above two things, I think we should instead make those two lines:\r\n\r\n```css\r\nbackground-color: Canvas;\r\ncolor: CanvasText;\r\n```\r\n\r\n(`background-color` instead of `background` because it's cheaper and shouldn't be observable, but...)\r\n\r\ncc @nt1m @futhark",
